  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history shows sustained positive sentiment (e.g., >0.5) and model overestimates prices.",
    "Reduce forecast magnitude by 5-10% if recent true outcomes show mean reversion after a spike.",
    "Increase forecast lag by 1-2 days if sentiment history indicates delayed market reaction.",
    "Apply downward bias correction when model forecasts peak after a sharp upward sentiment spike.",
    "Use sentiment history to weight forecast adjustments: higher sentiment = higher downward correction factor.",
    "Avoid over-optimistic forecasts when sentiment is neutral or negative (e.g., <0.3)."
  ]
